cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Swift corpus or models, cite this work. Citing BANKING77 alone is not
  sufficient attribution: BANKING77 supplies the English text and the intent labels, which
  is 20% of the rows and one of the three label columns. The four other language tracks,
  the sentiment and priority label columns, and the frozen split are this project's.
title: >-
  Swift: A Multilingual Support-Ticket Triage Corpus and Baselines for Sinhala, Tamil and
  English, Including Romanized Code-Mixed Text
type: dataset
authors:
  # Names confirmed. TWO THINGS ARE STILL ASSUMPTIONS, both flagged rather than decided:
  #  - ORDER: repository owner first.
  #  - WHICH NAME IS THE FAMILY NAME. Written here as Seneviratne / Sutharsan / Shaheed.
  #    Sri Lankan Tamil and Muslim naming does not always put the family name last, so if
  #    "Ruththiragayan" or "Shazan" is the family name, swap the fields — otherwise
  #    citations will render "Sutharsan, R." and "Shaheed, S." incorrectly. The BibTeX on
  #    the cards encodes the same assumption (BibTeX reads the last token as the surname).
  - family-names: Seneviratne
    given-names: Sithija
  - family-names: Sutharsan
    given-names: Ruththiragayan
  - family-names: Shaheed
    given-names: Shazan
year: 2026
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: https://huggingface.co/Swift-Support
repository-artifact: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Swift-Support/swift-support-tickets-1.0
keywords:
  - support-ticket triage
  - Sinhala
  - Tamil
  - code-mixed
  - romanized text
  - intent classification
  - low-resource NLP
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Efficient Intent Detection with Dual Sentence Encoders
    authors:
      - family-names: Casanueva
        given-names: Iñigo
      - family-names: Temčinas
        given-names: Tadas
      - family-names: Gerz
        given-names: Daniela
      - family-names: Henderson
        given-names: Matthew
      - family-names: Vulić
        given-names: Ivan
    collection-title: >-
      Proceedings of the 2nd Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Conversational AI
    start: 38
    end: 45
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.18653/v1/2020.nlp4convai-1.5
    notes: BANKING77 — source of the English text and the 77-way intent labels.
